      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by:\n\n1. **Never storing it in the Hub\u0027s environment** \u2014 A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup, but does not put it into the Hub\u0027s own process environment.\n\n2. **Injecting it only into child processes** \u2014 The key is injected directly into the environment of spawned agent child processes (like the Ingest or Query agents) immediately before they start, not inherited from the Hub.\n\n3. **Keeping it short-lived** \u2014 The credential exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API.\n\nThis design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key never lives there.",
      "input_tokens": 4305,
      "output_tokens": 193
    }
